# The pure count of each test file: how many pure items the pure stage (ci/test.sh) counts in it. Pure items are
# the tests the stage runs, less those it skips because a module it hides (qgis, PyQt5, PyQt6, sip, osgeo) stops
# them. One line per test file with at least one pure item: the number, a space, the file. The stage fails when a
# file's count differs from its line, or a file is in only one of the two; it reads this file from the tested tree.
# A change that adds pure tests adds or raises their file's line. The total may only rise: a change that lowers it
# needs the maintainer's approval in its pull request. The stage compares each file with its line in the tree it
# tests, never with an earlier commit, so that rule is kept in review.
